WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.210
- [Narrator] Jo Jorgensen
is the Libertarian Party's

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.550
nominee for president in 2020,

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.150
and the only candidate on
the ballot in all 50 States,

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.180
other than Donald Trump and Joe Biden.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.490
A recent NPR poll showed
her pulling 5% nationally,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.070
which could cover the spread between

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.570
the President and his challenger.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.520
According to a chorus of
pundits and partisans though,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.130
voting for a third party
candidate is a waste,

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.880
because it doesn't change
the high-stakes battle

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.580
to either toss out or keep in
office Donald Trump in 2021.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:35.260
- This is not the time to
withhold our votes and protests

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:38.740
or play games with candidates
who have no chance of winning.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.150
- [Narrator] Jorgensen,
a 63-year-old Clemson

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.230
psychology lecturer, is
running on a blend of standard,

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.170
small government rhetoric
disgust with career politicians,

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.830
optimism about young people,

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.220
and of course the occasional craziness

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.910
that we all expect from
third party nominees.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.270
- I am running for
president because government

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:59.629
is too big, too bossy,
too nosy, too intrusive.

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:03.160
But the worst part is,
they usually end up hurting

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.740
the very people they're trying to help.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.560
- [Narrator] She says
that most of her followers

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.130
are either Independents
or first time voters.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.850
And that the real mistake would be

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.520
to vote for Trump or Biden.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:16.310
Particularly in parts of the
country where a principled vote

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.810
is unlikely to impact the final outcome.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.751
- I would say if you're in a
solidly red state, like I'm in,

00:01:21.751 --> 00:01:24.570
if you don't like what
Donald Trump has been doing,

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.490
if you don't like the bigger
government he's given you,

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.650
then voting for him is a wasted vote.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.010
And to Democrats, especially
Democrats in California,

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.641
in New York, don't vote for Joe Biden,

00:01:36.641 --> 00:01:38.370
vote for what you really want.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.030
- [Narrator] Jorgensen who ran
as the LPs vice presidential

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.290
nominee back in 1996, wants
to bring all the troops home,

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.340
cut the size of government
in half, legalize drugs,

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.590
and in our interview, suggested replacing

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.730
Ruth Bader Ginsburg on the Supreme court

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.520
with someone like
82-year-old Alan Dershowitz.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.930
Though she later recanted
on social media because

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.310
of his statements that torture
may sometimes be acceptable,

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:02.930
his opposition to gun rights,

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.970
and what she called unresolved questions

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.553
about his association
with Jeffrey Epstein.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.710
Jorgensen says that
Republicans have failed

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:14.800
to live up to their promises
of fiscal discipline.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.830
- A lot of people don't realize
that government grew year

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:21.260
after year after year for eight
straight years with Reagan.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.167
People keep saying,

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.630
"Oh, look at Donald
Trump, we got tax cuts."

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.350
Well yeah, but he increased spending,

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:29.660
so the bill is eventually
going to come due.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.827
He came in saying, "I'm a businessman,

00:02:31.827 --> 00:02:33.027
"I know how to balance a budget,

00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:36.122
"I know how to cut spending",
and he didn't do that.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:40.430
And not only did he not cut
spending, he increased spending.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.980
Now we've got a bigger
deficit, bigger debt.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.980
Whether you're talking education,

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:48.410
healthcare, retirement,
it all boils down to,

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.130
are you in control of your dollars?

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.830
- [Narrator] Biden, says Jorgensen,

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.930
has shamelessly pandered to
voters for nearly 50 years.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:58.410
- People wanted to hear
him say I'm tough on crime,

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.060
so he said, I'm tough on crime.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.940
And now they want to hear something else,

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.750
so he's something else,
he doesn't have a rudder.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.540
He doesn't have something
that's guiding him.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.990
That's true not only about Biden,

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.470
but pretty much any Democrat out there.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:15.200
Young people are shocked to
hear that both Hillary Clinton

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.351
and Barack Obama were
against gay marriage,

00:03:18.351 --> 00:03:22.630
just back in 2012, that
was only eight years ago.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.830
- [Narrator] Speaking of young people,

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.650
Jorgensen is big on Gen Z.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:28.820
Arguing that young Americans
are less about cancel culture

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:32.200
and being woke and more
about being Laissez-faire.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.720
- They go, well, why shouldn't
you be able to own a gun?

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.890
Why shouldn't two people
the same sex get married?

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.665
If you can drink red wine,
why can't you smoke marijuana?

00:03:40.665 --> 00:03:43.690
So, that overall they have

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:46.860
a very libertarian underpinning

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.570
as far as their kind of live and let live

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.830
libertarian philosophy,
so that's excellent news.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.920
If I could sit around the kitchen table

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.250
of every American family in this country,

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.500
I would win by a landslide.

